meta {
  name: Set Item Verdict
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/deal-audits/{{reviewItemId}}/verdict
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{auditReviewerToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "verdict": "pass",
    "note": "Matches the application."
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("records the ruling and who made it", function () {
    const review = res.getBody().item.review;
    expect(review.verdict).to.equal("pass");
    expect(review.note).to.equal("Matches the application.");
    expect(review.reviewedAt).to.be.a("string");
    expect(review.reviewedByName).to.be.a("string");
  });

  test("a pass verifies the item", function () {
    // The manager's verification is the stronger fact, and the only way a
    // manager-only item ever closes.
    const item = res.getBody().item;
    expect(item.isResolved).to.equal(true);
    expect(item.open).to.equal(false);
  });

  test("returns the page's running tally", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.counts.passed).to.be.at.least(1);
    expect(body.unmet).to.be.an("array");
    expect(body.canApprove).to.equal(body.unmet.length === 0);
    expect(body.canSendBack).to.equal(body.counts.failed > 0);
  });
}

docs {
  # PATCH /deal-audits/:itemId/verdict — the manager rules on one item (PAC-106)

  The Pass / Fail toggle and the note box on each checklist row of the Deal
  Audit page.

  - **Module:** `deal_audits`
  - **Permission:** `deal_audits:write` **and** `management:read`.
  - **Data scope:** the item's audit must be in the caller's reach; else `404`.

  Only while the audit is **Pending** (`409` otherwise — a sent-back audit is
  the producer's until they resubmit), and never by the person who submitted it
  (`403`).

  ## Body
  At least one field.

  | field   | type | rules |
  |---------|------|-------|
  | verdict | `"pass"` \| `"fail"` \| `null` | `null` withdraws a ruling. Omitted leaves the ruling as it is — so the page can save a note on its own. |
  | note    | string | ≤ 2000 chars, trimmed. `""` clears it; omitted leaves it. On a `fail` it is what the producer reads. |

  ## Effect
  - Stores `reviewVerdict`, `reviewNote`, `reviewedAt`, `reviewedById` on the
    item — **beside** the producer's `isResolved` / `notes`, never instead of
    them: the producer's claim and the manager's verification are two facts.
  - **`pass` resolves the item** (`isResolved: true`, *Verified - Complete*),
    keeping an existing `resolvedAt`. It is the only way a manager-only item
    closes, so without it the audit's open-items count never reaches zero.
  - **`fail` changes nothing else yet** — the item reopens for the producer
    when the manager sends the audit back (**Review Audit**,
    `request_changes`).
  - Withdrawing a pass (`null`) does not un-resolve the item; the Approve gate
    reads verdicts, never `isResolved`.
  - Recomputes the audit's roll-up counters. Idempotent.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "item": {
      "id": "665f...ac1",
      "itemName": "Good Student",
      "category": "Auto",
      "subjectName": null,
      "producerVisible": true,
      "requiresUpload": true,
      "open": false,
      "isResolved": true,
      "resolvedAt": "2026-10-14T10:00:00.000Z",
      "producerNote": "Transcript attached.",
      "attachments": [],
      "review": {
        "verdict": "pass",
        "note": "Matches the application.",
        "reviewedAt": "2026-10-19T15:01:00.000Z",
        "reviewedByName": "Morgan Manager"
      }
    },
    "counts": { "passed": 7, "failed": 0, "remaining": 0 },
    "canApprove": true,
    "canSendBack": false,
    "unmet": []
  }
  ```

  `item` is the same shape as **Get Deal Audit Review**'s `items[]`; the page
  swaps it in place and updates the summary bar from the rest.

  ## Errors
  - `400 Bad Request` — neither field sent, an unknown verdict, or a note over
    2000 characters.
  - `403 Forbidden` — missing `deal_audits:write` or `management:read`, or the
    caller submitted this audit.
  - `404 Not Found` — no such item, it belongs to an older audit of the deal,
    or it is out of reach.
  - `409 Conflict` — the audit is not awaiting review.
}
